---
import Layout from "../../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import RegressionSim from "../../../components/simulations/RegressionSim.astro";
---

<Layout
  path="/teaching/data-science-fundamentals/regression"
  title="Regression, Cost and Gradient Descent: Interactive Lab — Ahmad Fathan Hidayatullah"
  description="Interactive lab on linear regression, the cost function, gradient descent and logistic regression, explained in plain English with ten made-up students."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Data Science Fundamentals · Regression"
    title="Regression, from a prediction to a learning process"
    lede="One path through four ideas: fit a line, measure its error, let the model learn from that error, then turn the answer into yes or no."
  />

  <div class="container-site py-10">
    <nav class="mb-6 text-sm text-muted" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/teaching" class="font-medium text-primary hover:text-primary-dark">Teaching</a>
      <span class="mx-1.5">/</span>
      <a href="/teaching/data-science-fundamentals" class="font-medium text-primary hover:text-primary-dark">Data Science Fundamentals</a>
      <span class="mx-1.5">/</span>
      <span>Regression Lab</span>
    </nav>

    <RegressionSim />

    <section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">How to use this page</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted marker:text-primary">
        <li><b class="text-ink">1. Linear regression</b>: move the two sliders to try a line, then press <i>Find the best line</i> to see what OLS picks.</li>
        <li><b class="text-ink">2. Cost function</b>: the same ten scores, now scored as a single number. <i>J = MSE / 2</i>, and smaller is better.</li>
        <li><b class="text-ink">3. Gradient descent</b>: press <i>One step</i> to follow the arithmetic, or <i>Run</i> to watch the parameters walk downhill.</li>
        <li><b class="text-ink">4. Logistic regression</b>: a yes/no target. The straight-line score becomes a probability, then a decision.</li>
        <li>The scores in sections 1 to 3 are shared: edit one and the other two follow. Section 4 keeps its own pass/fail labels, because those are a different dataset.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
